TEXT -200 128 Left 2 !.tran 0 7s 0 0.6ms
TEXT -200 136 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=10 abstol=100m reltol=0.003
TEXT 224 184 Left 2 ;General:\n \nThis model is a synchronous generator without transformer and regulation of voltage and speed\nThe speed is regulated externally\nThe voltage is regulated externally\n \n \n \nparams:\n            UN_verkettet=20000 Nominal voltage\n            IN=14.434k Nominal current\n            Pel=400e6 Nominal power (UN_verkettet*IN*cosphi of 0.8)\n            Kc=0.5 short-circuit ratio (0.5 cylindrical pole, 0.8-1.0 salient pole)\n            UE0=600V Nominal field voltage\n            IE0=2000A Nominal field current\n            p=2 Number of poles      \n            Schenkelpolfactor=0.5 for salient pole machine (kc=0.8-1.0)\n                                              1 for cylindrical pole machine(kc=0.4-0.5)                                                             \n             Daempferfaktor=1 (damping factor)\n             Streuung=0.05 (leakage factor)\n             rcu=0.01 (rel. Copper resistance)\n             rbg=0.001 (rel. friction moment)\n             J=100000 (inertia)\n             n0=1500 starting speed\n             err0=0 (best do not change this)\n             a=0.9 parameter for nonlinear saturation\n             m=7 parameter for nonlinear saturation\n             n0=1500 Starting speed\n             err0=0 (if full starting voltage but set starting timepoint in .TRAN card approx. 10ms to prevent spikes)\n \nAlternative Elements: none\n          \nHINT: The power output can be computed with M*314.159/2  (P=M*omega/p)\n                    The load angle can be outputed with V(u1:u1:theta) \n                    The here constant frequency is n/30    2*n/60 = p*n/60 (p=Polcount)\n \nLibfile: Sgen.lib
TEXT -480 144 Left 4 ;Generator at a island\n(isolated networkwithout voltage source)
TEXT -184 328 Left 2 ;For voltage regulation there is a AVR\nIt is enabled from 3.5s because then the\ngenerator output voltage reach their nominal\nvalue. You can see that the voltage drops at\nswitching the load and later is compensated\nby increasing the field voltage of the machine
TEXT -264 472 Left 2 ;Speed regulator is on at from the beginning\nAt 4s there is a load step of 100MW\nsee load angle V(u1:u1:theta) of approx. 8 degrees
TEXT -384 264 Left 2 ;Internal load angle =  V(u1:u1:theta)
TEXT 80 384 Left 2 ;After 4s there is a load step \nof 100MW
TEXT 80 368 Left 2 !.param PN=100e6 QN=0
TEXT -320 536 Left 2 ;Torque
TEXT -240 536 Left 2 ;Friction torque
TEXT -96 288 Left 2 ;3.5s
TEXT -112 272 Left 2 ;4.0s
TEXT -128 256 Left 2 ;20000v
TEXT -416 464 Left 2 ;1500
TEXT -288 496 Left 2 ;1
TEXT -256 184 Left 2 ;Kp=0.05 Tn=0.1 Min=200 Max=1800  U1Nenn=20k verr0=600
TEXT -400 176 Left 2 ;P-Part of controller set small ->\nbecause of voltage ripple \n(Test it )
TEXT -16 424 Left 1 ;New since Version 2.5 for the SG with externals controls:\nAdditional parameters of LDx LDy LE L0 RDx RDy R0 can be set\nat the model paramterline: \nIf not set the parameters are set to default values: \nLDx,LDy,LE,L0  to Ls (stray of stator)\nRDx,RDy,R0 to Rs(resistance of stator)\nThis is done according to the parameter computation (see wxmaxima file)\nfrom the generator datasheet values: \nXd,Xq,Xd',Xq', .....  Td0,Td'' ......
